{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-40310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the negative infinite geometric sequence that has a third term equal to $-1$ and a seventh term equal to $-\\frac{1}{4\\,096}.$ What is the sum to infinity of the terms of this sequence?\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that $4\\,096={8}^{4}.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-40310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFrom the question statement we have ${a}_{3}=-1$ and ${a}_{7}=-\\frac{1}{4\\,096}.$ We can find the common ratio using the following formula:\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in the known information into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{7-3} & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{4\\,096})}{(-1)} \\\\ {r}^{4} & =\\frac{1}{4\\,096} \\\\ {r}^{4} & ={(\\frac{1}{8})}^{4} \\\\ r & =\\sqrt[4]{{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{4}} \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we have taken the positive fourth root since we're told that the sequence is negative.\n\nNow, using the formula\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1}\n$$\n\nfor the $n$th term of the geometric sequence, we can find the first term. Indeed, for $n=3$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{2} \\\\ -1 & ={a}_{1}{(\\frac{1}{8})}^{2} \\\\ -1 & ={a}_{1}(\\frac{1}{64}) \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{-64}{(1-\\frac{1}{8})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{64}{(\\frac{7}{8})} \\\\  & =-64\\cdot \\frac{8}{7} \\\\  & =-\\frac{512}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-40310" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "105cf3c2f5db117c048b7427008694961f488ad8662a66615506c4500b32bb89"} {"question" "q-40310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-40310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{224}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{27}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{32}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{512}{7}"] ["math" "-\\frac{64}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-40310" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{512}{7}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-75627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the sum to infinity of the geometric series $6.4+4.8+3.6+2.7+⋯$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-75627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=6.4$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{4.8}{6.4}=0.75.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{6.4}{1-0.75} \\\\  & =\\frac{6.4}{0.25} \\\\  & =25.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-75627" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "105cf3c2f5db117c048b7427008694961f488ad8662a66615506c4500b32bb89"} {"question" "q-75627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-75627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "19.2"] ["math" "21.8"] ["math" "25.6"] ["math" "27.3"] ["math" "30.2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-75627" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "25.6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-124570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the positive infinite geometric sequence that has a first term equal to $9$ and a third term equal to $4.$ What is the sum to infinity of the terms of this sequence?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-124570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFrom the question statement we have ${a}_{1}=9$ and ${a}_{3}=4.$ We can find the common ratio using the following formula:\n\n$$\n{r}^{n-m}=\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}}\n$$\n\nSubstituting in the known information into the above gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{3-1} & =\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ {r}^{2} & ={(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\ r & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we have taken the positive square root since we're told that the sequence is positive.\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{(1-\\frac{2}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{(\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =9\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-124570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "105cf3c2f5db117c048b7427008694961f488ad8662a66615506c4500b32bb89"} {"question" "q-124570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-124570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "18"] ["math" "27"] ["math" "33"] ["math" "36"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-124570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "27"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-347769" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of the geometric series \n\n$$\n8-0.4+0.02-0.001+⋯.\n$$\n\n Do not round the answer.\n\n${S}_{\\infty }=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-347769" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=8$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{-0.4}{8}=-0.05.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{1-(-0.05)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{1+0.05} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{1.05} \\\\  & =\\frac{800}{105} \\\\  & =\\frac{160}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-347769" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "105cf3c2f5db117c048b7427008694961f488ad8662a66615506c4500b32bb89"} {"question" "q-347769" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-347769" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{160}{21}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-353146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of the geometric series \n\n$$\n1.5+1.2+0.96+0.768+⋯.\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n${S}_{\\infty }=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-353146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum to infinity ${S}_{\\infty }$ of a geometric series is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{\\infty }=\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r},\\,|r|<1,\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term and $r$ is the common ratio.\n\nFor the given geometric series, the first term is ${a}_{1}=1.5$ and the common ratio is\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}}=\\frac{1.2}{1.5}=0.8.\n$$\n\nSo, using the formula, we find that the sum to infinity is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{\\infty } & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{1-r} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{1-0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.2} \\\\  & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-353146" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "105cf3c2f5db117c048b7427008694961f488ad8662a66615506c4500b32bb89"} {"question" "q-353146" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"} {"question" "q-353146" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7.5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973527/state.json" "file_sha256" "110fb12cb03c3feb3fb8d0f11ba549c6ae682d68cb2a3ef20502bf41831af53d"}] "usage" {} "basis" 676 "retractions" [] "immuta